        "username": "LeperKhan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/leperkhan/{size}/1894_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-06-14T04:23:01.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Thanks for the info about .hack! Hadn't heard about that yet, so had to search it up after reading.</p><p>If Mario Odyssey is really so huge like they claim it is, then I guess that it will be enough to tide fans over until the next big release. The sheer magnitude of Breath of the Wild has definitely kept me from finding a lot of things thus far, and I'm not about to fight the final boss until I have several more shrines under my belt! Mario won't be that big, surely, but they've touted it as being the most expansive Mario game, so I hope it really live up to that. I may not like the concept of Mario wandering around next to normal looking people when he is so cartoonish...or the realistic dinosaur when we obviously know that dinosaurs have a saddle and long tongues...but it's still an instant buy for me because it's a main entry.</p>",
