        "id": 198728,
        "name": "LeperKhan",
        "username": "LeperKhan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/leperkhan/{size}/1894_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-06-15T04:02:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You're right! I guess I'm a little more hesitant about that one because there's not really anything to compare it to. Like...does it just mean a top down Pokemon game with 3d graphics, like Sun and Moon...or does it mean a full-fledged 3d title with wild Doduos running through the plains as you bike by, dodging the peck attacks of the Spearows that are chasing you while fumbling at your belt to grasp at the pokeball containing that quickly-evolved starter that you fell in love with? A 'port' of Sun and Moon (labelled Stars) does not interest me as much as a full, complementary, ground-up Switch RPG.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
